    "q-275711": {
      "dom_id": "step-q275711",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/a2efe530287edefcee1609c5765d84c9608c5680f80a056819692f80a2e8c0f9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{mm}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law of addition for $a$ and $b.$ We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane. The resultant goes from the start of $a$ to the head of $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/41bd69400fe98c2f8ab964c76fa295a6624f83d51fc720ba251ae4c618f87954.png)\n\nNow, in $△AHB,$ we have $m∠AHB={90}^{∘},$ $AH=30\\,\\text{mm},$ and $BH=10\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{900+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1000} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|a+b|=10\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{mm}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
