    "q-317060": {
      "dom_id": "step-q317060",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/29e3f8ef81b98c4073e934a59f59557d399d105991c2386c3178c3840bd6ac3a.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, where $|a|=5\\sqrt{3}$ and $|b|=6,$ find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/c58fcaace0fd6b1161426357025da18aaccd182b7035db152221bdfddbe28226.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b{|}^{2} & =|a{|}^{2}+|b{|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =(5\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{6}^{2}-2\\cdot (5\\sqrt{3})\\cdot 6\\cdot \\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =75+36+90 \\\\  & =201.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{201}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
